<!--
doc/src/sgml/ref/cypher_delete.sgml
PostgreSQL documentation
-->

<refentry id="cypher-delete">
 <indexterm zone="cypher-delete">
  <primary>DELETE</primary>
 </indexterm>

 <refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>DELETE</refentrytitle>
  <manvolnum>7</manvolnum>
  <refmiscinfo>SQL - Language Statements</refmiscinfo>
 </refmeta>

 <refnamediv>
  <refname>DELETE</refname>
  <refpurpose>removes vertices or edges</refpurpose>
 </refnamediv>

 <refsynopsisdiv>
<synopsis>
[ DETACH ] DELETE <replaceable class="parameter">expression</replaceable> [ , ... ]
</synopsis>
 </refsynopsisdiv>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Description</title>
  <para>
    The <command>DELETE</command> clause is a clause that removes vertices or edges.
  </para>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Parameters</title>
  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry>
    <term><literal>DETACH</literal></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      If the DETACH keyword is used together, the edges associated with the vertices are
      also removed. If the vertices you want to remove are linked to other vertices and edges,
      you may skip the edge-removing process.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry>
    <term><replaceable class="parameter">expression</replaceable></term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Find the vertices or edges that you want to remove through the MATCH clause. 
      See <xref linkend="cypher-expr"/> for more details.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Examples</title>

  <para>
   Find the vertices you want to remove through the MATCH clause and remove them by
   marking corresponding variables in the DELETE clause.
<programlisting>
MATCH (m:person {name: 'Michael'})
DELETE m;
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   Find the edges you want to remove with the MATCH clause and remove them by
   marking corresponding variables in the DELETE clause.
<programlisting>
MATCH (m:person {name: 'Michael'})-[l:likes]->(b:person {name: 'Bella'})
DELETE l;
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   To find a property:
<programlisting>
MATCH (j {name: 'Jack'})
RETURN j.age;
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   Delete a vertex with all its relationships
<programlisting>
MATCH (m:person {name: 'Michael'})
DETACH DELETE m;
</programlisting>
  </para>
 </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
  <title>See Also</title>
  <simplelist type="inline">
   <member><xref linkend="cypher-match"/></member>
  </simplelist>
 </refsect1>
</refentry>

